# Capture to Obsidian

<!-- capture-to-obsidian:start -->
- Obsidian capture directory: `{{OBSIDIAN_CAPTURE_DIR}}`
- Apply the installed `capture-to-obsidian` skill to this dedicated capture
  project. If the directory is missing or still contains the placeholder, run
  the skill's setup workflow and ask for a path in the user's language.
- Treat every user message without another explicit task as a new Obsidian note.
  This includes ordinary or dictated text, URLs, UUIDs, long numbers, Codex task
  or chat IDs, document IDs, and similar resources.
- If the user explicitly asks not to record something, do not save it. If the
  user requests both capture and another task, do both.
- Resolve readable links and identifiers before recording. Preserve user-authored
  source messages and exclude assistant replies unless requested.
- After setup, tell the user in their language that they can drop any link, ID,
  or dictated message into the conversation for automatic capture. After each
  normal capture, reply only with the created file link.
<!-- capture-to-obsidian:end -->
